# L §5.5, E §3.1 step 5 and E §3.3: the cone of an ask follows the item graph; a place's flows and a balance read the
# timeline, whose axis options are those of the axes the moves reach. pay books amt into konto, and amt reads the axis
# mode (L §5.11: alt beats base when mode == b), so flows(konto, 2026) is amt_a = 10.00 PLN under a and amt_b =
# 20.00 PLN under b (L §5.18 Lines: one line per distinct result across the axes reached); bal(konto, 2026-12-31)
# likewise, from the opening 0.00 PLN. (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §5.5: axis mode read outside the axes the ask
# reaches; a fault found by running a text.)
=== m.tally
model p12
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

axis mode
  a "first reading"
  b "second reading"

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input amt_a: money PLN
input amt_b: money PLN
input pay_day: date

def amt: money PLN at reader
  rule base = amt_a
  rule alt beats base = amt_b when mode == b

move pay: transfers
  on pay_day
  at pay_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

ask q: flows(konto, 2026) law 2026-06-30
ask bl: bal(konto, 2026-12-31) law 2026-06-30

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  amt_a = 10.00 PLN
  amt_b = 20.00 PLN
  pay_day = 2026-03-01
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
=== expect
bl [mode = a]: 10.00 PLN
...
bl [mode = b]: 20.00 PLN
...
q [mode = a]: 10.00 PLN
...
q [mode = b]: 20.00 PLN
...
